{start_of_verse: Verse 1}
A great eagle with [C#]wings so wide
Came down to Le[D#m]banon's pride
Took the top of the cedar [C#]tree
Carried it to a foreign [D#m]see
Planted it in merchant [C#]soil
Beside the water, low and [D#m]toil
It grew a vine with branches [C#]spread
Its roots reached out as it [D#m]fed
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: Verse 2}
But another eagle stood near[C#]by
With thick and heavy plumage [D#m]dry
The vine bent its roots toward [C#]him
Seeking water in his [D#m]rim
It had good soil and [C#]rain
To bear fruit without vain [D#m]strain
But it turned to a second [C#]king
And broke the sacred, holy [D#m]thing
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I will take a sprig from the [C#]top
From the lofty cedar's [D#m]crop
And plant it on a high [C#]mountain
Where the birds in shade are [D#m]wanting
It will become a ma[C#]jestic tree
Where all the birds shall [D#m]be
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: Verse 3}
The king of Babylon came [C#]strong
Took the crown and led it a[D#m]long
Made a covenant with the [C#]prince
Swore an oath for the de[D#m]fense
But he rebelled and sent en[C#]voys
To Egypt for horses and [D#m]toys
He broke the oath and despised the [C#]vow
In Babylon he shall now [D#m]bow
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus: Chorus}
I will take a sprig from the [C#]top
From the lofty cedar's [D#m]crop
And plant it on a high moun[C#]tain
Where the birds in shade are want[D#m]ing
It will become a ma[C#]jestic tree
Where all the birds shall [D#m]be
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_bridge: Bridge}
I bring down the high and lift [C#]the low
I make the dry and dead [D#m]tree grow
All the trees of the field [C#]will know
That I, the Lord, am the [D#m]power
{end_of_bridge}

{start_of_verse: Outro}
I, the Lord, have [C#]spoken and will do
On the height of the land, it is [D#m]true
{end_of_verse}

